##-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Modelled on tidelink/cdc/tidelink_top.prj, which is a working driver.
##
## Invocation (see cdc/README.md §2 for the full environment):
##   $SPYGLASS_HOME/bin/spyglass -batch \
##       -project $CHIPLET/cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.prj \
##       -goals "cdc/cdc_verify" < /dev/null
##
## The `< /dev/null` is not decorative — Genus, Innovus and the SpyGlass shell
## all hold a licence seat at an interactive prompt if stdin stays open.
##
## Environment consumed (all set by the README's export block):
##   FLIST   filelist to read
##   SG_TOP  elaboration top
##   SGDC    constraints file
##   SWL     waiver file
##-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## -- Design read --------------------------------------------------------------

# The integration RTL is SystemVerilog-2009; the SoC and the CMSDK/XHB500
# collateral are mixed Verilog/SV.
set_option enableSV09 yes
set_option language_mode mixed
set_option designread_enable_synthesis no

# The chiplet is substantially larger than tidelink_top alone (two Cortex-M0+
# cores, the DAP, DMA-230, the MAC, the HA1588 PTP unit and the whole D2D link).
# tidelink_top.prj uses 50000; raised here so elaboration does not truncate.
set_option mthresh 200000

# PREREQUISITE: the filelist below `-f`-includes two GENERATED sub-flists,
#   build/chip/flist/soc.flist
#   build/chip/flist/tidelink_asic.flist
# and the generated wrapper build/chip/rtl/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_chip.v. Render
# them first (see cdc/README.md §2) or the read fails on a missing file rather
# than on anything to do with CDC.
#
# It also carries `+define+TIDELINK_PHY_V2`
# (build/chip/flist/tidelink_asic.flist:3), which the SGDC depends on — three
# axi_chiplet_controller ports exist only under that define. See the
# BUILD-CONDITIONAL PORTS block in cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sgdc §7a before
# pointing this at a different filelist.
read_file -type sourcelist $::env(FLIST)

## -- Elaboration --------------------------------------------------------------

# Default nanosoc_eth_chiplet — the INNER top, where the clocks are still
# distinct ports. Not nanosoc_eth_chiplet_chip: that wrapper aliases rtc_clk and
# user_ref_clk onto sys_fclk and leaves role_locked_o open. Full argument in
# cdc/README.md §1.
set_option top $::env(SG_TOP)

## -- Constraints --------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE file, deliberately. tidelink_top.prj reads three SGDCs (its own plus
# axi_chiplet_controller.sgdc and xhb500.sgdc); this project keeps the
# black-box port constraints inside the single chiplet SGDC instead, because
# those two TideLink files carry TideLink's own period set (hclk 4.0,
# link_rx_clk_o 64.0) and reading them here would put two contradictory sets of
# clock periods into one run. Their port lists had also fallen eleven ports
# behind the RTL this build compiles — see cdc/README.md §4.
read_file -type sgdc $::env(SGDC)

## -- Waivers ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nearly empty on purpose. Read cdc/waiver.swl before adding anything to it.
read_file -type waiver $::env(SWL)

## -- Black-boxed IP -----------------------------------------------------------
# stop_module prevents SpyGlass from tracing INTO these modules, so CDC analysis
# sees only their port-level constraints (the abstract_port blocks in
# cdc/nanosoc_eth_chiplet.sgdc §7).
#
# THE COST OF THIS OPTION IS NOT ZERO. Every port of a stopped module that has
# no abstract_port gets a DEFAULT domain, and a defaulted port on a black box is
# how you manufacture a crossing that does not exist
# (tidelink/cdc/axi_chiplet_controller.sgdc:69-79 records two of them). So a
# module goes on this list only when its full port set has been enumerated
# against the RTL, or when it is single-clock and can be wildcarded honestly.
#
#   axi_chiplet_controller
#       TideLink's Wlink-based D2D controller. Ports enumerated and verified
#       against tidelink/src/rtl/local_overrides/axi_chiplet_controller.sv
#       (the copy build/chip/flist/tidelink_asic.flist:187 actually compiles).
#
#       ---- B8: REMOVING THIS IS A ONE-LINE CHANGE -------------------------
#       The plan un-black-boxes this module as a SEPARATE, LATER step, once the
#       baseline with it stopped is established and understood. To do it:
#       delete the token `axi_chiplet_controller` from the stop_module line
#       below. Nothing else changes — the §7a abstract_port block becomes inert
#       (SpyGlass applies port constraints only to stopped/undefined units) and
#       the controller's ~6800 lines, including the a2l replay CDC and the
#       recovered-RX-clock domain, enter the analysis.
#       Expect the run to get substantially longer and the report to grow. Do
#       NOT do it in the same change as anything else, or you will not know
#       which findings are new crossings and which are new constraints.
#       ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   xhb500_ahb_to_axi_bridge_chiplet_slv / xhb500_axi_to_ahb_bridge_chiplet_mst
#       Arm XHB500. Single-clock (`clk`), so `abstract_port -ports "*"` onto one
#       domain is honest rather than a shortcut.
#
#   rf_01k / rf_08k / rf_16k / rf_32k
#       TSMC65 compiled register files. Their Verilog models are in no filelist
#       this build reads, so SpyGlass already treats them as undefined modules;
#       listing them makes that explicit and stable.
set_option stop_module {axi_chiplet_controller \
                        xhb500_ahb_to_axi_bridge_chiplet_slv \
                        xhb500_axi_to_ahb_bridge_chiplet_mst \
                        rf_01k rf_08k rf_16k rf_32k}

## -- NOT black-boxed, and why -------------------------------------------------
# The brief for this setup named "Arm CMSDK/CoreSight" as black-box candidates
# alongside XHB500 and the memories. They are deliberately LEFT ELABORATED, and
# this is the one place this project departs from that instruction.
#
# The reason is the asymmetry stated at the top of the SGDC: a wrong constraint
# masks, an absent one only over-reports. Stopping a module obliges you to
# constrain every one of its ports, and the two candidates here cannot be
# wildcarded honestly:
#
#   CM0PDAP (cm0p_dap_top.v / CM0PDAP.v) is a genuinely TWO-DOMAIN block — SWD
#   probe clock on one side, fabric clock on the other. `abstract_port -ports
#   "*" -clock <one clock>` would collapse the swclktck<->sys_hclk boundary into
#   a single domain and DELETE the most important debug-path crossing in the
#   design from the report. Its port list has not been enumerated, so the
#   alternative — a verified per-port split — is not available yet either.
#
#   CORTEXM0PLUS has FCLK/HCLK/DCLK/SCLK plus debug-side pins whose domain
#   membership has not been checked here.
#
# Leaving them elaborated costs runtime and produces extra INFO lines. It also
# means their vendor CDC cells (cm0p_dap_ap_cdc.v, cm0p_dap_dp_cdc.v,
# cm0p_dap_cdc_capt_sync.v) come back as RECOGNISED synchronisers, which is the
# result you actually want from a first pass.
#
# If the baseline run is intractably slow, the honest fix is to enumerate
# CM0PDAP's ports and add a verified two-domain block to the SGDC, then add it
# here. It is NOT to wildcard it onto one clock.
#
# The single-clock CMSDK leaf cells (cmsdk_ahb_to_apb, cmsdk_ahb_to_sram,
# cmsdk_apb_slave_mux) are also left elaborated: they are small, they carry the
# real APB/AHB paths of the two integration bridges, and black-boxing them would
# put a defaulted-domain boundary in the middle of this repository's own logic.

## -- Goal ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Specified via -goals on the command line, which is required in -batch
# -project mode. current_goal / run_goal are not used in that flow.
